The archives in this folder were made on macOS 27.0.1 with its /usr/bin/xar
(xar 1.8dev), pkgbuild and productbuild, from small files written for the
tests (text, a few kilobytes of patterned bytes, an empty file, a symbolic
link, a hard link, extended attributes, a name with "é & <>"):

  default.xar        xar -c (gzip, SHA-1)
  none-sha256.xar    xar -c --compression=none --toc-cksum=sha256 --file-cksum=sha512
  bzip2-sha512.xar   xar -c -j --toc-cksum=sha512
  coalesce.xar       xar -c --coalesce-heap --link-same (data shared by files)
  subdoc.xar         xar -c -n info -s subdoc.xml (a subdocument in the TOC)
  tiny.pkg           pkgbuild --ownership recommended, of one file
  product.pkg        productbuild --package tiny.pkg

Then the owner's user name was replaced by "nobody" in each table of
contents, which was compressed again with zlib, and its checksum written
again. Nothing else was changed. They are under the repository's license:

